{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire TV Stick 4K feels like a plausible next choice because my HDMI cable and Raspberry Pi setup suggest an interest in convenient media playback.",
    "The wireless earbuds connect to my history of choosing headphones while offering a useful way to listen away from my desk."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The smart displays, speakers, lighting bundle and smart plug assume I want home automation, while my purchases mostly address specific computer, connectivity and desk needs.",
    "The Ring charging station has no clear use without compatible equipment, and the whole-home camera bundle introduces a security project I have not shown an interest in.",
    "The older Fire TV Stick fits my media interests, but I would choose the 4K option here rather than buy two devices for the same purpose."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying electronics seems to have been taken as interest in almost any connected household device, even when it serves a different purpose.",
    "My Kindle and other Amazon purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to recommend Alexa products, although those purchases do not establish a need for voice control."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My cable management, Ethernet accessories, headphone mount and computer duster point toward maintaining and improving a practical desk setup.",
    "Accessories need to work with equipment I actually use; a shared electronics connection is not enough to make a specialized charger useful.",
    "My headphone history supports another listening option more directly than it supports a household smart speaker."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in electronics and listening, but stretched it into smart-home needs that my practical computer and desk purchases do not establish."
}"}
